1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,240
Who is the student's best critic?
谁是这位学生的最佳评论家？

2
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:18,210
Who is the student's best critic?
谁是这位学生的最佳评论家？

3
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:25,060
I am an art student and I paint a lot of pictures.
我是个学艺术的学生，画了很多画。

4
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:31,090
Many people pretend that they understand modern art.
许多人装作很懂现代艺术。

5
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:35,310
They always tell you what a picture is 'about'.
他们总是告诉你一幅画“讲的是什么”。

6
00:00:35,330 --> 00:00:40,500
Of course, many pictures are not 'about' anything.
当然，有很多画什么“讲”的也不是。

7
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:44,640
They are just pretty patterns.
它们就是些好看的图案。

8
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:50,840
We like them in the same way that we like pretty curtain material.
我们喜欢它们，就像喜欢好看的窗帘布一样。

9
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:59,470
I think that young children often appreciate modern pictures better than anyone else.
我认为小孩子往往比任何人都更能欣赏现代画。

10
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:01,910
They notice more.
他们观察到的东西更多。

11
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,450
My sister is only seven,
我的妹妹只有7岁，

12
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:10,210
but she always tells me whether my pictures are good or not.
但她总能说出我的画是好还是不好。

13
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,550
She came into my room yesterday.
昨天她走进我的房间。

14
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:18,460
'What are you doing?' she asked.
“你在干什么？”她问。

15
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:26,260
'I'm hanging this picture on the wall,' I answered. 'It's a new one. Do you like it?'
“我正把这幅画挂到墙上，”我回答说，“这是一幅新画，你喜欢吗？”

16
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,190
She looked at it critically for a moment.
她用挑剔的目光看了一会儿。

17
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:39,950
'It's all right,' she said, 'but isn't it upside down?'
“还可以，”她说，“不过是不是挂倒了？”

18
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,250
I looked at it again.
我又看了一遍。

19
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:44,280
She was right! It was!
她是对的！画确实挂倒了！
